{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-114198",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We proceed to factor the left side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36{d}^{3}-81{d}^{2}-16d+36 & = \\\\ (36{d}^{3}-81{d}^{2})-(16d-36) & = \\\\ 9{d}^{2}(4d-9)-4(4d-9) & = \\\\ (4d-9)\\cdot 9{d}^{2}-(4d-9)\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ (4d-9)(9{d}^{2}-4) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(4d-9)(9{d}^{2}-4)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(4d-9)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4d-9 & =0 \\\\ 4d & =9 \\\\ d & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(9{d}^{2}-4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{d}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ 9{d}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ d & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $d=\\frac{9}{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{2}{3}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
